# Conventional Commits Skill Development

When working on the commits plugin, the skill definitions are the source of truth — do
not duplicate their workflows here.

- **Message/commit skill**: [`plugins/commits/skills/conventional-commits/SKILL.md`](mdc:plugins/commits/skills/conventional-commits/SKILL.md)
  (format lives in its `references/format-reference.md`; judgment calls in `best-practices.md`)
- **Splitting skill**: [`plugins/commits/skills/commit-splitter/SKILL.md`](mdc:plugins/commits/skills/commit-splitter/SKILL.md)
  (atomic-commit analysis and hunk-level staging)
- **Commands**: [`plugins/commits/commands/`](mdc:plugins/commits/commands/) — `/commit`, `/commit-push`, `/commit-split` delegate to the skills

Format essentials: `<type>[optional scope]: <description>`, types
feat/fix/docs/style/refactor/perf/test/build/ci/chore/revert, breaking changes via `!`
or `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer. Full spec in the skill's format reference.
